# Approved Android 0.9.57 local signing preparation

The signed APK job verified all native code and the app's package identity,
but GitHub signing secrets were never configured for this project. The
established previous release process uses the original private signing backup
stored in ChatGPT Library to sign locally.

This one-time trigger builds and uploads only a verified unsigned Lab 0.9.57
APK and official Android SDK signing tools. The original private keystore
must not be copied to GitHub or included in any artifact.

The resulting APK will be signed outside GitHub, verified against the
unchanged original Lab signing certificate and delivered as an installable
update. This does not deploy the PWA.
